INT. MATTRESS SHOWROOM - NIGHT

Ninety beds in perfect rows. A neon sign: SLEEP KINGDOM. Rain on the roll-up door. One security light, buzzing.

A MAN in a bathrobe (50s, slippers, a thermos of soup) sits on the edge of a king-size display, staring at the ceiling.

GUARD DESHAWN (30s, polyester uniform, flashlight) enters from the back office. Stops. Raises the flashlight.

GUARD DESHAWN
Sir.

The man waves without looking.

MAN
Evening.

GUARD DESHAWN
Sir. We are closed.

MAN
I know.

GUARD DESHAWN
How did you get in?

MAN
Ordered a delivery. Left the door ajar. Your driver was very nice.

GUARD DESHAWN
You can't be here.

MAN
I haven't slept in six weeks. Do you know what that does to a person?

GUARD DESHAWN
No.

MAN
It does something. Not good. I keep seeing a man in the corner of the room. Turns out it's a coat rack. But the point stands.

GUARD DESHAWN
Sir. I will have to call someone.

MAN
Call whoever you like. Let me just try this one for ten minutes.

GUARD DESHAWN
It's a three-thousand-dollar mattress.

MAN
Hence the ten minutes.

GUARD DESHAWN
I'm going to need your name.

MAN
Gilbert.

GUARD DESHAWN
Gilbert what?

GILBERT
Gilbert Ferreira-Whitlock. Hyphenated, a long story, involves a cousin.

GUARD DESHAWN
Mr. Whitlock.

GILBERT
Ferreira-Whitlock. The hyphen is the whole point.

GUARD DESHAWN
Gilbert. My shift ends at six.

GILBERT
Then we have six hours.

GUARD DESHAWN
You don't have six hours. You have until I call my manager.

GILBERT
Your manager is Brenda. Brenda told me, and I quote, "he's a sweetheart, let him sleep."

GUARD DESHAWN
When?

GILBERT
Tuesday. At the open house. I do not remember it clearly but I trust Brenda.

GUARD DESHAWN
There is no open house on Tuesday.

GILBERT
Then it was a dream. A very restful dream.

GUARD DESHAWN
Gilbert, please.

GILBERT
Deshawn. May I call you Deshawn? It says Deshawn on the tag.

GUARD DESHAWN
It says GUARD DESHAWN on the tag.

GILBERT
That's what I said.

GUARD DESHAWN
You said Deshawn.

GILBERT
It's a lovely name.

Deshawn sits on the next bed over. Springs sigh. He puts the flashlight on his knee.

GUARD DESHAWN
My mother had a bed like this.

GILBERT
Did she sleep well?

GUARD DESHAWN
She did.

GILBERT
There. You see.

Gilbert lies down in his robe, hands folded on his chest. He closes his eyes.

GILBERT (CONT'D)
Don't leave. I might wake up.

GUARD DESHAWN
Ten minutes.

GILBERT
Ten minutes.

Deshawn lies back. The neon buzzes. The rain keeps on.

Two snores, nearly in unison.
